--- A helper's parameter carries a derivative where a call hands it one
--- (`shown[sum[x]]`), and the helper is then held to what the tape
--- differentiates, as the function differentiated is; the same helper
--- handed a size alone (`shown[float[len[x]]]`) is any builtin's
use math

fn shown[v]
    return str[v * 2.0]

fn loss[x]
    size = shown[float[len[x]]]
    twice = shown[sum[x]]
    if size eq '4'
        return sum[x .* x]
    return sum[x]

log[grad[loss][tensor[[1.0, 2.0]]]]
